
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<section class="rd-privacy-page">

    <div class="rd-privacy-hero">
        <span class="rd-privacy-eyebrow">RACEDAY SA</span>
        <h1>Your privacy matters.</h1>
        <p>
            Learn how RaceDay handles the personal information you provide
            when using our event platform.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rd-privacy-content">

        <div class="rd-privacy-intro">
            <span class="rd-privacy-label">PRIVACY &amp; DATA</span>
            <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p>
                RaceDay SA is an event management platform that allows
                participants to discover and enter sporting events, and
                organisers to manage events and related information.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rd-privacy-section">
            <h3>1. Information We Collect</h3>
            <p>
                When you register for or use RaceDay, you may provide
                personal information such as:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>First name and last name.</li>
                <li>Email address and contact number.</li>
                <li>Account login information.</li>
                <li>Profile pictures, if uploaded.</li>
                <li>Event enrolment and participation information.</li>
                <li>Results and other information associated with events.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rd-privacy-section">
            <h3>2. How We Use Your Information</h3>
            <p>
                Information provided through RaceDay may be used to:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Create and manage user accounts.</li>
                <li>Allow participants to browse and enter events.</li>
                <li>Help organisers manage events and enrolments.</li>
                <li>Display relevant event and participation information.</li>
                <li>Maintain and improve the platform.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rd-privacy-section">
            <h3>3. Account Security</h3>
            <p>
                Users are responsible for keeping their account credentials
                confidential. RaceDay should use appropriate security
                measures to protect account information and prevent
                unauthorised access.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rd-privacy-section">
            <h3>4. Information Sharing</h3>
            <p>
                Personal information should only be accessed or shared where
                necessary to provide the platform's services, support event
                administration, or meet applicable legal requirements.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rd-privacy-section">
            <h3>5. Data Storage and Retention</h3>
            <p>
                Information submitted through RaceDay may be stored
                electronically. Personal information should only be retained
                for as long as necessary for its intended purpose or as
                required by applicable law.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rd-privacy-section">
            <h3>6. Your Responsibilities</h3>
            <p>
                Users should provide accurate information, keep their
                account details secure and contact the platform
                administrator if they identify incorrect information or
                have concerns about their personal data.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rd-privacy-section">
            <h3>7. Changes to This Policy</h3>
            <p>
                This policy may be updated as RaceDay develops. Any revised
                version should be made available on this page.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rd-privacy-contact">
            <h3>Questions about your privacy?</h3>
            <p>
                For questions or concerns about personal information
                submitted through RaceDay, please contact the platform
                administrator.
            </p>
            <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index" class="rd-btn-primary">
                Back to Home
            </a>
        </div>

    </div>

</section>
